ght search terms to use when tackling  a bug that they were encountering I know  I still have problems with that as a  native English speaker so there's an  added layer of complexity there for some  people a lot of people mentioned reading  issue threads and pull requests wasn't  worth it  because there was too much slang  involved in those threads that  convoluted the discussion and made it  really difficult for them to follow the  developer I was just talking about Anna  was also mentioning that when she would  read documentation she would have to  double-check with her coworkers  do I not understand this because it's  poorly written or jus not I not  understand this because of a gap in my  English proficiency right so this was  another check that people had to do for  themselves in order to understand  whether or not it was them or something  that was pre-written poorly we all know  how much documentation is written poorly  out there and how many bad resources  there are out there so I can't imagine  having that additional challenge yes by  far one of the biggest barriers for  people seemed to be community  involvement and the judgment that came  along with that so I think everyone here  can agree that community involvement is  so essential for your growth and your  learning and enjoyment and success in  the industry right in your career and  it's such a vital part of being involved  in this industry that it's a shame that  people feel start to feel left out of it  some people mentioned that they would  have a hard time following a technical  conversation not because they weren't  skilled enough or because they didn't  have the technical knowledge but simply  because it would be a large group of  people talking very fast about a  particular topic and that made it  challenging for them to follow along  which made it look as if they didn't  know what people were talking about my  friend Belen mentioned that she produces  materials in English like screencasts  and articles and talks and sometimes  people will question her materials or  her technical prowess her skill set  because of a spelling or grammar mistake  or or her accent very simple things and  there's this added layer of having to  prove yourself now if you have this  barrier  that most of us are unfamiliar with  right so a lot of people did say some  positive things about their community  involvement but overall the tone felt  kind of lonely and I think this is  something that we should definitely be  working on as an industry and based on  some of the responses that I was getting  there were definitely some things that  stood out to me that we could start  doing and things that people mentioned  so one of those was when you're creating  resources try to use more illustrations  and charts and graphs those are more  Universal and often helped clarify  things we're written text falls short  Lin Clark got a really great shout out  from one of the respondents for all of  the work that she's been doing there so  if we could all make an effort to do  something more like that I think that  would be super helpful limiting the  slang that we use in issues and PR  threads if we can aim for words that  might be translated more easily in other  languages it might feel silly at first  it might feel robotic at first but it  would help break down some barriers for  certain developers that I think would be  super helpful and then lastly we need to  be working with native speakers of other  languages to create these resources to  create better resources more Universal  resources and I'm not exactly sure just  what this looks like yet but I'm hoping  to collect more data and more  experiences so that we can figure that  out so I'm sure a lot of people here  have dealt with some of these issues  they've experienced these things I would  love to hear from all of you if you have  I plan on keeping my survey open  indefinitely so that people can continue  to respond to it so I'll tweet that out  in a little bit but any experiences that  you have anything that you think that we  can be doing to alleviate some of these  difficulties that were causing for other  developers I would love to talk with you  more about that okay feel free to find  me during the breaks or after all the  talks will be around today if you have  any insights or experiences you want to  share or maybe even some other terms and  origin stories that you find really  interesting I'd love to hear about them  hope you enjoy the rest of the  conference thank you  [Applause]
 

